v0.12.0 — a flat-rate lane and a voice: OpenCode Go joins DeepSeek / GLM / OpenAI-compatible as a $10/month subscription, `seek serve` gains push-to-talk (record → DeepSeek ASR → a real conversation), sub-agents can run in the background and be woken by id, MCP servers get namespaced tools plus prompt guidance, and DeepSeek's document API plus an opt-in safety check land behind config. The kernel also starts shedding weight in public: a `-tools` whitelist and a read-only friction report are the first v8 cuts you can measure.

Notable changes:

- OpenCode Go lane (new). `--provider=opencode` speaks the OpenCode Go subscription ($10/month, request-window quota over an open-weight pool). seek self-identifies with its own `User-Agent` and a per-session `x-opencode-session` header — without it the lane silently degrades to per-token billing. Lane default model is `deepseek-v4.1-flash`; the first-run wizard, the sub-agent routing table and the pricing card (indicative per-token only) all learned it, and `--base-url` now overrides the endpoint for GLM and opencode too.
- Push-to-talk (new). `seek serve --frontend=web --frontend=voice` adds a mic button to the web page: hold, speak (≤120 s), release — the clip is transcribed by DeepSeek ASR (billed per second) and enters the plane as its own conversation `voice:<device-id>`, bindable with `/bind` like any other. Browsers need a secure context (localhost works; front it with HTTPS over a tailnet). The TTS broadcast side ships as a `Speaker` building block with pricing and tests; it has no CLI switch yet.
- Document input (new). `@report.pdf` uploads through the DeepSeek Files API: routing happens at submit (copy-at-submit; the local asset library keeps the only copy), a reused `file_id` keeps the prefix cache warm, and `@rich:` asks for layout-rich parsing. Replayed turns show the file marker dimmed. `read_url` was measured against function tools in the R0 gate and deliberately NOT wired — the two cannot coexist in one request.
- `safety_check` (new, opt-in). Set it to `high` and the DeepSeek lane sends the model-safety parameter; a refusal comes back as a normal turn instead of an error.
- MCP deep integration (behaviour change). Tools register as `server__tool` by default (`semble__search`); `mcp.json`'s `prefix: false` keeps bare names when they are free, and a collision still falls back to the prefixed form. A new sysprompt `MCPSection` segment (per-session static; empty segment is byte-identical to before) carries `hint` / `mcp_prompt` guidance, and server registration order is now deterministic.
- Sub-agents: background + resume. `run_in_background` sub-agents' completion events flow into the main session (status badge, `/agents` MODE column); `session_id` revives one with its context and lineage intact; `-resume` back-fills completed-but-unnotified children so a completion is never lost.
- Typed agent definitions. SKILL.md-style files under `~/.seek/agents/` and `<project>/.seek/agents/`, frontmatter shared with skills; `seek agents list/check/create/remove` is the only write path; per-type tool whitelists plug into the permission layer; the three built-in templates (explore / judge / general) carry default lanes.
- Hooks expansion. New observer points (SubagentStart/Stop, Stop, PreCompact, Notification) plus shell events; `pre_prompt_inject` is an opt-in single-seam injection channel (2048 B default / 8192 B cap, truncation marker, injected bytes audited) with a guard test that the prompt-prefix segment stays byte-identical.
- ACP completeness. `session/new` returns `configOptions`, `session/set_config_option` switches models at runtime, `SEEK_ACP_PROVIDER` / `SEEK_ACP_MODEL` pin them; `tool_call` now carries kind/locations/rawInput/rawOutput/content, reasoning streams as `agent_thought_chunk`, and a text content block no longer poisons the whole frame — results travel in `rawOutput` only.
- Web workbench W0–W4. Streaming chat (delta accumulation, collapsible tool rows), a sessions browser (cursor-paged), memory and stats views, a background sub-agent task panel (SSE tail-follow), `?token=` → cookie exchange with Origin/Host gates on writes, plus CSP, gzip and a size gate in CI.
- Thin-kernel knobs and measurement. Top-level `-tools` whitelist (frozen at startup; unknown names exit 2); read-only `stats/friction` over `/rpc` (per-tool errors / denials / repeats folded from the transcript); `scripts/kernel-deps.sh` dependency-direction report; `eval/ablate.sh` bare-core vs full dual run; selftest now discovers scripts automatically; autopilot Outcome carries tokens/cost and diffstat.
- Fixed: `list_dir`'s default-depth output now names the `depth=2` re-call in-band (the root cause of `bash-overreach`'s coin-flip); `seek agents remove` validates the name before touching the filesystem; worktree GC gained an age fallback; session / subagent IDs widened 24 → 64 bits of entropy; `seek session export` renders a transcript to markdown.
- Quality: eval gained the ablate dual-run lane and a trend radar, plus two recalibrated cases (bash-overreach now bounds "bash never first" ordering; code-review-effort-max's runaway ceiling was raised to match its measured range); subtraction cuts 4 and 5 removed orphan read/write paths (including `sandbox.Wrap` on linux/other); 29 delivered PRDs moved to `docs/prd/archive/`.
